From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Grische <github@grische.xyz>
Date: Fri, 14 Aug 2026 22:23:37 +0200
Subject: MIPS: intel-mips: enable USB host support in grx500_defconfig

The whole USB menu was off. Turn on the host stack the FRITZ!Box 7560's
port needs: the dwc3 core in host mode, xhci-plat underneath it, the
generic PHY framework and the new GRX500 USB PHY, and the Lantiq reset
controller the PHY's reset line comes from.

RESET_LANTIQ has no prompt outside COMPILE_TEST and defaults to
SOC_TYPE_XWAY, which INTEL_MIPS does not select, so it is reachable only
by selection. PHY_INTEL_GRX500_USB now selects it in its own right;
stating it here as well keeps the dependency visible to anyone reading
the defconfig.

REGULATOR and REGULATOR_FIXED_VOLTAGE are both required, and neither is
reachable by select: VBUS on this board is a regulator-fixed on a GPIO,
and a driver that consumes a supply only calls the consumer API. Left
off, they fail in two different ways, which is worth stating separately
because the symptoms share no diagnostic:

 - REGULATOR=n replaces the consumer API with stubs.
   devm_regulator_get_optional() then answers -ENODEV unconditionally,
   which is indistinguishable from a board that declares no
   vbus-supply at all, so the PHY takes its "port power is fixed"
   branch; regulator_enable() returns 0 without touching the line.
   The PHY probes clean, the controller starts, and the port is dead
   with nothing logged above dev_dbg. This is the dangerous one: it
   looks exactly like a VBUS wiring fault.

 - REGULATOR=y with REGULATOR_FIXED_VOLTAGE=n leaves the vbus-supply
   node in DT with no driver to register a provider for it.
   of_regulator_dev_lookup() finds the node, finds no regulator_dev
   and returns -EPROBE_DEFER (drivers/regulator/of_regulator.c), and
   _regulator_get_common() passes any error other than -ENODEV through
   unchanged, so the PHY defers forever instead. Visibly stuck, not
   silent.

Nothing in the polarity handling depends on this choice. The gpiolib-of
quirk that makes enable-active-high, rather than the phandle's flag
cell, define the line's polarity for regulator-fixed nodes is compiled
out along with REGULATOR_FIXED_VOLTAGE, but it only ever runs on the
path where the symbol is on -- it is a statement about what the DT
means, not a third reason to enable it. The board DTS states both
consistently regardless.

USB_XHCI_PLATFORM and GENERIC_PHY are implied by USB_DWC3 and
PHY_INTEL_GRX500_USB respectively and are stated anyway, as
CONFIG_PHY_INTEL_GRX500_PCIE's neighbours already are, because a
defconfig that names what it depends on survives being read.

No mass-storage stack. SCSI, BLK_DEV_SD, USB_STORAGE, the NLS
codepages and VFAT/EXT4 are all absent, deliberately: what a router
image mounts off a stick is a packaging decision, and OpenWrt makes it
with modules. The kernel-side milestone is enumeration.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5
Signed-off-by: Grische <github@grische.xyz>

diff --git a/arch/mips/configs/grx500_defconfig b/arch/mips/configs/grx500_defconfig
index 98f812230054..6f35d44c323b 100644
--- a/arch/mips/configs/grx500_defconfig
+++ b/arch/mips/configs/grx500_defconfig
@@ -96,9 +96,16 @@ CONFIG_PINCTRL_EQUILIBRIUM=y
 CONFIG_POWER_RESET=y
 CONFIG_POWER_RESET_SYSCON=y
 # CONFIG_HWMON is not set
+CONFIG_REGULATOR=y
+CONFIG_REGULATOR_FIXED_VOLTAGE=y
 # CONFIG_VGA_CONSOLE is not set
 # CONFIG_HID is not set
-# CONFIG_USB_SUPPORT is not set
+CONFIG_USB_SUPPORT=y
+CONFIG_USB=y
+CONFIG_USB_XHCI_HCD=y
+CONFIG_USB_XHCI_PLATFORM=y
+CONFIG_USB_DWC3=y
+CONFIG_USB_DWC3_HOST=y
 CONFIG_NEW_LEDS=y
 CONFIG_LEDS_CLASS=y
 CONFIG_LEDS_GPIO=y
@@ -110,7 +117,11 @@ CONFIG_LEDS_TRIGGER_NETDEV=y
 # CONFIG_MIPS_PLATFORM_DEVICES is not set
 CONFIG_INTEL_CGU_CLK=y
 # CONFIG_IOMMU_SUPPORT is not set
+CONFIG_GENERIC_PHY=y
 CONFIG_PHY_INTEL_GRX500_PCIE=y
+CONFIG_PHY_INTEL_GRX500_USB=y
+CONFIG_RESET_CONTROLLER=y
+CONFIG_RESET_LANTIQ=y
 # CONFIG_MANDATORY_FILE_LOCKING is not set
 CONFIG_QUOTA=y
 # CONFIG_PRINT_QUOTA_WARNING is not set
